The table header is `| Named test path |` (**L4166**) with delimiter `|---|` (**L4167**), i.e. a **one-column** table. All **55** data rows (**L4168–L4222**) carry **two** cells, e.g. L4168 `| \`tests/hooks/test-graphify-gate.sh\` | Named test (see Design coverage map) |` and L4222 `| \`tests/scripts/test-universal-silver-migrate.sh\` | Named test (see Design coverage map) |`. Under GFM, cells beyond the header count are **discarded**, so the entire second column — including the two distinguishing annotations `(see Design coverage map; absorbed omni)` at **L4180 / L4181 / L4193** — does not render. This is the only column-count-inconsistent table in the document (all other tables are internally consistent). Not a product fork; a freeze-consistency/rendering defect in an appendix inventory the charter treats as canonical. Distinct from closed F-03 (which was inventory *completeness* vs Appendix B / §5.4, not column arity).

### LOW-2 — Unterminated inline-code span at L4122 inverts code/prose rendering for the remainder of the Appendix A history cell

**L4122** (the single-line "Revised (full prior cell)" table cell in `### A. SHA lineage and round receipts`, L4114ff) contains an **odd** number of backticks (1153). The defect is at the Round-24-era PUB-01 clause, which reads:

> `PUB-01 must not promote before current-generation \`comp_val_two_clean\` (order \`comp_val_two_clean → promote → \`comp_val_verified\`; …`

The closing backtick after the second `comp_val_two_clean` is missing, so the span opens at `` `comp_val_two_clean → promote →  `` and the intended literal `comp_val_verified` is rendered as prose while the following prose is rendered as code. Because the parity flip is never corrected, **every** subsequent code/prose alternation on that line (~570 further spans, through the end of the cell) renders inverted. L4122 is the **only** line in the document with unbalanced backticks outside fenced blocks. Scope is archival round history (explicitly "Do not treat round history as a second architecture", L4120), which caps severity at LOW; the surrounding round receipts are still normative provenance.

